{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "c9fbb4f4-61d0-8695-a6de-3c1c691ee565",
  "created_at": "2025-12-05T11:26:39-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Nelson Moniz",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:22:36-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:22:40-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi Tony. Nelson Moniz here. I got a shutoff warning in the mail for my water and sewer, and I'm, uh, not thrilled about it. I want to know how much time I got."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:22:52-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, sorry about that. Let me pull you up. What's the service address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:22:57-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "156 Rhode Island Avenue, up the Hill. I'm the renter there, but the water bill comes to me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:23:04-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, give me one second. [pause] Okay, I see the account. There's a past due balance and a notice went out. Do you have the letter in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:23:15-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I got it right here. Sorry, you're on speaker, I'm doing like three things at once. Can you hear me okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:23:23-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine. Look at the letter, there should be a date on it, something like pay by or shutoff date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:23:31-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, hold on. It says, pay on or before December nineteenth to avoid discontinuation of service. That's two weeks from today, basically."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:23:39-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, that matches what I see. So you've got until the nineteenth to pay the past due amount, and that keeps the water on. It's the past due portion they're looking at, not necessarily everything that's been billed since."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:23:53-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Because I honestly thought I was caught up. It's wicked annoying, I paid something back in the fall."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:24:00-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I do see a payment in the fall. It looks like it covered the older bill but then the next quarter's bill came after and that one's still open."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:24:10-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ahh, so it's the new one. Okay. That I get. Still, a little notice would've been nice before a shutoff letter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:24:18-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I hear you. The bill itself went out, and this is the reminder that follows when it's not paid. Happens a lot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:24:26-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. Now, my daughter helps me with all the bills, she's way better at it than me. Can I get her put on the account so she can call and ask about it? Instead of me being on speaker with a letter in my hand."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:24:42-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, we can do that. Since the account's in your name, we'd need you to authorize her. Easiest is for you to send in something written with your name, the address, and her name and phone number, signed. Or you can come by the office."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:24:58-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, written is fine. Can I email it or does it have to be paper?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:25:04-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Drop it off or mail it in to start. If you want to know about email, I can have somebody confirm that for you, but paper works for sure."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:25:14-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Paper, okay. Alright. And here's the other thing. I work during the day, so getting to City Hall before it closes is a pain. Is there a drop box or something where I can leave a payment after the office is closed?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:25:29-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there's a payment drop box at City Hall. You can leave a check or money order in it anytime, and it gets picked up the next business day. Just put your account number or the service address on the check, and don't leave cash."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:25:45-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. So if I put it in Monday night, it counts for the nineteenth, no problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:25:51-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Monday's way ahead of the nineteenth, you're fine. I'd just not wait until the last night."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:25:57-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, no, I'm not going to cut it close. Not after this letter. [pause] Sorry, it's really starting to come down out there. I just bought a new umbrella and haven't even had a chance to test it. Guess today's the day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:26:12-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it's a good day for it. Stay dry out there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:26:17-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Will do. So, to recap, nineteenth is the deadline, drop box for after hours, and a signed note for my daughter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:26:25-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. Put her name and number in the note, and your account address. Anything else I can look at for you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:26:33-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nope, that's it. Thanks, Tony."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-05T11:26:36-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Nelson. Take care."
    }
  ],
